   "id": "menachot.108b.3",
   "daf": "108b",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "״שְׁנֵי שְׁוָורִין אֵלּוּ עוֹלָה״ וְנִסְתָּאֲבוּ, רָצָה יָבִיא בִּדְמֵיהֶן אֶחָד, וְרַבִּי אוֹסֵר. מַאי טַעְמָא?",
   "en": "The mishna teaches that if one says: «These two bulls are» hereby «a burnt offering, and they became blemished,» if «he wishes he may bring with» the «money» of «their» redemption «one» bull. «And Rabbi» Yehuda HaNasi «deems» this «prohibited,» and holds that he must bring two bulls. The Gemara asks: «What is the reason» that Rabbi Yehuda HaNasi deems it prohibited to bring only one bull?"
  }
